#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: KHAN
#> pause: 45
#> must: In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
#> must: In Xanadu did Kubla KHAN
#> must: Down to a sunless sea.
#> not: pleasure dome
#> not: Where Alph
#> source: /KHAN/p
# 13. p and w write the line as it is at that moment. McMahon 3.3
# With -n, nothing is written unless p or w says so. /Khan/p writes line 1
# before the s changes it; /KHAN/p writes it again afterwards, so the same
# input line appears twice, differently. w <file> writes selected lines to a
# file (ten files at most; exactly one space after w); $w sends the last line.
# Try: move /Khan/p below the s line: it no longer matches, so one copy less.
#ARGS -n
/Khan/p
s/Khan/KHAN/
/KHAN/p
$w /dev/stdout

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
